# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages. Static assets and prerendered routes are
# matched first, so every public page still serves its own HTML with its own
# link-preview tags.
#
# The destination must be /index.html. Pages strips .html from a destination and
# turns it into a 308, so pointing this at Nuxt's empty /200.html shell instead
# resolves to /200, which then 308s to itself: an infinite loop on every URL,
# static assets included. /index.html is the one destination Pages special-cases.
#
# In practice this rule never fires. Measured against the deploy, Pages answers a
# route with no file of its own (/admin/students/s0, /tutor/classes/c0) with its
# own 404.html, which is the same empty Nuxt shell: the app boots and the router
# renders the right screen, only the status line says 404. Production has always
# behaved this way. The rule stays as the safety net for if that ever changes.
/*    /index.html   200
